  "slug": "right-sliding-drawer",
  "label": "Right sliding drawer",
  "description": "A non-modal quick view docked to the right edge, 550px wide, opened by clicking the body of a result card. The page behind it stays live and interactive: the selected card keeps its highlight and the filter rail keeps working. The header carries the item title, an optional primary action, and three icon buttons. The body scrolls independently and holds the item's summary, its pinned properties, and a tab bar whose panels are the same ones the full detail page shows.",
  "when": "Use when a user needs to inspect one item without losing the list they found it in. Do NOT use asset-detail-360: that is the full page this drawer previews, reached by clicking the item TITLE rather than the card body, and it carries tabs and sections the drawer omits. Do NOT use a modal for this: in the product a drawer and a modal are different surfaces, and the difference is not decorative. The drawer sets `::backdrop { display: none }` and is opened non-modally so the page stays usable behind it; the modal paints a 60% black backdrop and blocks the page. Reach for a modal when the user must answer before continuing, and for this drawer when they must not lose their place.",
