  "slots": {
    "header": "Item title, an optional subtitle holding the technical path, an optional primary action, and three icon buttons: favourite, open in full page, close",
    "tags": "Item type, catalog folder, connection, and a data quality indicator carrying a coloured traffic light",
    "summary": "A Summary heading with an information icon, over the item's description",
    "featured-properties": "A Featured properties heading over pinned label and value pairs, laid out as a definition list",
    "tabs": "A tab bar whose labels carry result counts, over the selected tab's panel"
  },
  "renderNotes": [
    "Do NOT compose this from `fmDialog`. It is a stub: it returns a hardcoded `<div class=\"fm-dialog__title\">Dialog</div>` and an empty body, reads no props at all, and cannot be given a title, an action or any content. The drawer is therefore composed from frames, TEXT and the components below. This is the same class of gap as the ones filed in plugin #299.",
    "`fmTabs` reads `Tabs` (a comma string or an array) and `Active`, and renders no count badge. The real drawer's tabs read `Fields 2`, `Properties 8`, `Contacts 4`, `Suggestions 0`, so the counts cannot be drawn. They are written into the tab label here so the count is at least visible, which is a workaround and not a fix.",
    "`fmIconButtons` renders an empty div carrying only a Type class, with no glyph inside. The favourite, open-in-page and close buttons therefore draw as blank squares. Do not read a blank square in the render as a missing node.",
    "Children of a VERTICAL frame must omit `sizing`. `sizing.horizontal:\"FILL\"` emits `flex:1`, which in a column container distributes height instead of hugging content. `faceted-browse` carried 20 of these against its own notes and `tests/app-context-recipes.test.js` now walks every skeleton for the case.",
    "This recipe composes the overlay surface ONLY, at its captured width of 550px. In the product the dialog is `position: fixed` with `inset: 70px 0 0 0`, so it docks to the right edge below the app header and runs to the bottom of the viewport. The page beneath is not part of this composition and stays interactive."
  ],
